WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.500
Plan the move as a sequence of supported states.

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.760
Begin with receiving and the intended loaded configuration.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.540
Follow the approved handling arrangement through doors, turns, lifts or ramps to

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:11.420
the final position.

5
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.040
Include temporary equipment and packaging wherever they affect the envelope or loads.

6
00:00:16.581 --> 00:00:20.380
The animation advances along the route and pauses at each evidence boundary.

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.640
A frame payload result doesn't establish a lift rating or floor point-load

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:24.980
limit.

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.200
A doorway clearance doesn't prove that a turn can be completed.

10
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.400
The handling method must remain within the supplied design's approved conditions.

11
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.820
At the final position, verify access for connection, isolation and replacement, not

12
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.160
only the occupied footprint.

13
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.760
Qualified site and handling teams must establish the actual procedure and limits.

14
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.660
For our review, preserve their acceptance evidence and any restrictions.

15
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.480
If a route segment is unresolved, hold the activity that depends on

16
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.600
it rather than allowing the rack's structural rating to stand in for

17
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:55.180
site approval.

